Alembic migrations for load-log.

The alembic_version table lives in the `load_log` schema (see env.py
VERSION_TABLE_SCHEMA), not `public`. The DB URL is built at runtime from the
POSTGRES_* environment variables.

Baseline note: revision 0001 creates the habits / habit_completions /
exercises / workout_sets tables in the load_log schema, but ONLY with
CREATE ... IF NOT EXISTS. So it is a harmless no-op on the production DB (where
those tables already exist, created by db.ensure_tables() and moved into the
load_log schema during the manual Phase 2 migration), and it builds the schema
from scratch on a fresh database (the local dev stack / cloners).

Because 0001 is idempotent, you do NOT need to stamp first — just run:

    uv run alembic upgrade head

The container entrypoint (docker-entrypoint.sh) does exactly this on startup.
(Stamping with `uv run alembic stamp 0001` is still harmless if you prefer to
be explicit on an existing DB.)
